---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

/* Required, not decorative: the alerts plane stores email addresses, and a
   double opt-in flow without a privacy notice is an incomplete one. Kept short
   because a notice nobody reads protects nobody. */
const title = 'Privacy — bagdex';
const description =
  'What bagdex stores, why, and how to have it deleted. Browsing is anonymous; '
  + 'the only personal data held is the email address on a price watch.';
---
<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <div class="page">
    <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/">Bags</a> <span>/</span> <b>Privacy</b>
    </nav>
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p class="note">
      Short version: browsing is anonymous, and the only personal data held is
      an email address you typed into a price watch.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Browsing</h2>
      <p class="note">
        The catalog is static files. No account, no login, no tracking pixels,
        and no advertising cookies. Your filter selections live in the URL and
        your theme choice in your own browser's local storage — neither reaches
        us.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Price watches</h2>
      <table class="spectable">
        <tbody>
          <tr><th scope="row">What we store</th><td>Your email address, what you asked to watch, and when.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Why</th><td>To email you when that price drops. Nothing else — no newsletter, no “related offers”.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Confirmation</th><td>Double opt-in. Nothing is ever sent to an address that has not clicked the confirmation link.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">How long</th><td>Until you unsubscribe. There is no other expiry.</td></tr>
          <tr><th scope="row">Deletion</th><td>One click in any email. It deletes the row outright — the address is gone, not flagged as inactive — and takes the record of what we sent you with it.</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="note">
        Addresses are never written into the public repository this site is
        built from, and never appear in application logs; those record a
        numeric subscription id instead.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Who else sees it</h2>
      <p class="note">
        Three processors, each doing one job: <strong>Supabase</strong> hosts the
        database the address sits in, <strong>Resend</strong> delivers the
        email, and <strong>Vercel</strong> serves the site. Resend keeps its
        own delivery log containing recipient addresses, as every email
        provider does — so unsubscribing removes you from our side immediately,
        but their log retains a record of past sends for a period we do not
        control. No data is sold or shared with anyone else.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your rights, and how to use them</h2>
      <p class="note">
        You can ask what we hold about you, ask for it to be corrected, or ask
        for it to be deleted, and there is no charge for any of it. Unsubscribe
        already does the deletion instantly. For anything else, write to
        <a href="mailto:privacy@bagdex.com">privacy@bagdex.com</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Product data</h2>
      <p class="note">
        Specifications and prices come from brands' own published product
        feeds. Nothing on this site is estimated, and every value records where
        it came from. If you operate a store, see
        <a href="/bot/">about the crawler</a>.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
